flowchart TD
  request[A person starts a build]
  triage[Triage by file type]
  archives[Archive expansion]
  binaries[Binary strings]
  skipped[Skipped and census]
  dedup[SHA1 dedup and prettify]
  lines[In-memory file lines]
  literal[(literal_index.json)]
  inverted[(inverted_index.json)]
  functions[(function_index.json)]
  renames[(rename_map.json)]
  strings[(string_table.json)]
  lazy[(Lazy caches)]
  zip[Index zip]

  request -->|CLI or Build dialog| triage
  triage -->|source files| dedup
  triage -->|zip tar gz har| archives
  triage -->|executables| binaries
  triage -->|media and unknown| skipped
  archives -->|entries, nested to depth 5| dedup
  binaries -->|pseudo-source| dedup
  dedup -->|unique files| lines
  lines -->|saved first| literal
  lines -->|line to files, skips common| inverted
  lines -->|tree-sitter plus regex| functions
  functions -->|infers display names| renames
  functions -->|string bounds| strings
  functions -->|built later, on demand| lazy
  zip -->|loaded instead of built| literal

%% tip: A person starts a build :: Nothing watches the source. An index stays as it was built until someone rebuilds it.
%% tip: line to files, skips common :: Lines under 4 characters, or found in more than 50 files, are not indexed. Searches that use this index can miss them.
%% tip: tree-sitter plus regex :: Per file, not either/or: regex runs too, and the results are merged.
